# Git & GitHub Strategy

## 1. Branch Strategy

| Branch | Scope | Role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **main** | Global | **Production**. Stable, deployable code. |
| **dev/be** | `itdaing/` | **Backend Staging**. Source of truth for API/DB. |
| **dev/fe** | `itdaing-app/` | **Integration Staging**. Absorbs Backend changes. |
| **test/fe** | `itdaing-app/` | **QA/Hotfix**. Experimental features & bug fixes. |

## 2. Sync Workflow

Maintain strict synchronization to avoid drift.

1.  **Main -> Backend:**
    - `git checkout dev/be`
    - `git merge --ff-only main` (After Prod Release)
2.  **Backend -> Frontend:**
    - `git checkout dev/fe`
    - `git merge --ff-only dev/be` (Regularly to get API updates)
3.  **Frontend -> QA:**
    - `git checkout test/fe`
    - `git merge --ff-only dev/fe` (Before starting new feature)

## 3. Commit Convention (Gitmoji)

Format: `[Gitmoji] [Type]: [Korean Description]`

| Emoji | Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| ✨ | `feat` | New feature |
| 🐛 | `fix` | Bug fix |
| ♻️ | `refactor` | Code restructuring |
| 💄 | `style` | UI/CSS changes |
| 📝 | `docs` | Documentation |
| 🔧 | `chore` | Config/Tooling |
| 🚀 | `deploy` | Deployment |

**Example:**
`✨ feat: 팝업 상세 페이지 퍼블리싱 완료`

## 4. Pull Requests (PR)

- **Title:** Same as Commit Convention.
- **Review:** At least 1 approval required.
- **Merge:** Squash & Merge preferred for clean history.
